strings |id, value|

bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_render_fractional_layout_followups_2026-11-28, 0, "1. Text on a line holding a vertical-align top / bottom box is 2 device rows high at k=4: 'ab <svg height=41 style=vertical-align:top>' Chrome paints ab on rows 23..70 of the line, Simple 21..68 (align_inline_line_device_dy returns 0 for has_valign; Chrome keeps the device baseline 70)."
    web_render_fractional_layout_followups_2026-11-28, 1, "2. An inline-block height:12.5px below the strut paints 13 rows at k=1: Chrome 5..16, Simple 4..16. The block return rounds the half px up; a box hanging from the whole-px baseline snaps its top. The svg path has the rule (hangs_from_baseline), the block return does not."
    web_render_fractional_layout_followups_2026-11-28, 2, "3. A clear block whose top margin is larger than the float is placed by its margin: float 30.75px, clear:both margin-top:40.5px as first in-flow child of a 50px block: Chrome puts it at the float's bottom (device row 1323 of a block at 1200), Simple at 1362."
    web_render_fractional_layout_followups_2026-11-28, 3, "4. Partly covered svg edge px are not blended: width=50 viewBox='0 0 3 1' at k=4, Chrome blends row 789 (about 0.63 coverage) and columns 89 / 288, Simple leaves them unpainted. A whole-px svg still rounds its viewBox edges (min-height:17px on the same svg: Chrome rows 483..548, Simple 482..549)."
    web_render_fractional_layout_followups_2026-11-28, 4, "5. <br clear> and a float inside an open line keep whole-px float edges (not measured against Chrome)."
    web_render_fractional_layout_followups_2026-11-28, 5, "6. width:40.5px max-width:40px on an svg after text starts one px right at k=1: Chrome columns 22..61, Simple 23..62 (the box takes the px of a fraction the clamp removed)."
    web_render_fractional_layout_followups_2026-11-28, 6, "7. Text inside a vertical-align:middle inline-block is 1 device row high at k=4 (2 rows before the middle fix; the box itself is on Chrome's rows)."

